  "body": "Found while fixing #1543.\n\nWhat happens: a Circular whose source is a pick (a round pocket's floor face, or a bore's rim) takes `DepthLaw::None` (`depth_law_of`, `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`), so its path is never judged against the part it was picked off. Reading: the `circular_pick.rs` fixture (a 40 x 40 x 8 block with a radius-15 round pocket, floor at Z 3), the floor face picked, Bottom typed Z 1: the rings cut to Z 1, 2 mm into the part under the floor, and the operation carries **0 warnings** (status ok, no `Warning::Gouge`, MCP `verify` lists no operation finding). Only the program-level post gate's stock sim catches it: `post blocked - gouge: program cuts below the model in 1202 cell(s), worst 2.00 mm at (-6.31, -8.31, z 1.00)`.\n\nSo the post is held (not a P1), but the operation reads clean, names no moves, and nothing holds it where the program sim is not run (a single op verify, the preview).\n\nExpected: a picked Circular is judged against the part like the picked pocket family and the picked Slot (#1504): `DepthLaw::Section` (or the shared `authored_law` of #1543 widened to picks), so the op itself carries the blocking Gouge on the moves under the floor; a legal picked circle (the existing `circular_pick.rs` cases) stays clean.\n\nWatch for: a typed-true circle against a coarse tessellated wall at stock-to-leave 0 is convicted by the chord sagitta under `Section` (see `docs/decisions/1543-circular-entity-law.md`); a pick hands the fitted circle, so the same read applies.\n\nDone means: a picked-floor Circular cut below its floor carries a blocking `Warning::Gouge` on the operation; the `circular_pick.rs` cases stay clean; MCP verify names the operation's gouge.\n\nRefs #1543\n",
